<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Muhammad al-Fasi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">16th century</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Muhammad al-Fasi was a sharif, said to have come from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a>, who around 1550 established himself in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fezzan">Fezzan</a> oases of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/libya">Libya</a> and founded the Awlad Muhammad dynasty. He made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/murzuq">Murzuk</a> his capital, and his descendants ruled the Fezzan as sultans, controlling the Saharan caravan route between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bornu">Bornu</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tripoli">Tripoli</a> until the early 19th century.</p></div>
